It looks like either the alpha autobuilder started up, or Steve
did some builds manually.  Either way, cool.  Also, a new libxml2
was uploaded, which restarts the 10-day clock, so it's less likely
that alpha is going to slow things down any.

However, it would still be nice if someone could get orbit2 to
build on alpha, as it's 9 days old and not blocked by anything else.
It could then go in tomorrow.  It looks like some builds failed
because orbit2 wasn't available (notably gconf2).

After orbit2 is built, the following packages would then be
the priority (built everywhere except on alpha, lots of things
depend on them):

libbonono
gconf2
gnome-vfs2
libgnome
libbonoboui



